        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Remove invalid `media` attribute from `<meta name="color-scheme">` docs]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45202</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45202"/>
        <updated>2026-08-17T21:26:10.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/185269030?u=1fc22565ccf4566b6f734fabaa87e03d9a31cfe4&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">Removes the incorrect <code class="notranslate">media</code> attribute entry from the <code class="notranslate">&lt;meta name="color-scheme"&gt;</code> documentation.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">The <code class="notranslate">media</code> attribute is only relevant for <code class="notranslate">&lt;meta name="theme-color"&gt;</code>, as documented on the main <code class="notranslate">&lt;meta&gt;</code> page. It was mistakenly also listed as a valid additional attribute for <code class="notranslate">&lt;meta name="color-scheme"&gt;</code>, likely copied over by mistake in a previous PR. This fix removes the incorrect mention so readers aren't misled into thinking <code class="notranslate">media</code> has an effect on <code class="notranslate">color-scheme</code>.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Related issues and pull requests</h3>
<p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #43091.">Fixes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3925502605" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43091" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/43091/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43091">#43091</a></p>]]></content>
